 In the docetaxel arm, $\kappa_0>1$ induces a monotone increasing hazard; in the nivolumab arm, $\kappa_1\approx1$ indicates an approximately constant hazard. The fitted log hazard ratio is time varying: $\alpha(1)=\AlphaCMOne$, it crosses zero near month \AlphaCMCross, and it reaches \AlphaCMTau\ at month \TauCM. This pattern is characteristic of immunotherapy and is consistent with the Schoenfeld diagnosis (Figure~\ref{fig:ph-diag}), whose negative residual slope indicates a decreasing log hazard ratio over time.
 
+For the design-stage evaluations that follow (theoretical ARE, empirical
+relative efficiency, power, and required sample size), we pair the fitted
+Weibull event-time model with a censoring working model informed by the
+trial design. Patients were enrolled between November 2012 and December
+2013, and overall survival was assessed at a database lock in March 2015,
+with a reported minimum follow-up of 13.2 months \citep{Borghaei2015}.
+Assuming approximately uniform accrual, we use the rounded administrative
+follow-up window $U\sim\mathrm{Uniform}(\CMAdminLower,\CMAdminUpper)$ months.
+We add an independent exponential dropout time
+$E\sim\mathrm{Exp}(\lambda_c)$ with $\lambda_c=\CMDropoutRate$ per month
+(about $\CMDropoutAnnualPct\%$ per year), and set $C=\min(U,E)$.
+The administrative window is consistent with the predominantly late
+censoring in the reconstructed data; the dropout rate is treated as a
+working design assumption and examined in the sensitivity analysis below.
 
